#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Luka and took the pilgrims home across the sea."
msgstr "Encontrasteis a Luka y llevasteis a los peregrinos a casa al otro lado del mar."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "In Ragusa, the bells ring for them."
msgstr "En Ragusa, las campanas suenan por ellos."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! The corsairs of Ulcinj took all our olive oil."
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}! Los corsarios de Ulcinj se llevaron todo nuestro "
"aceite de oliva."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "We traded it for the winter, and now we have nothing."
msgstr "Lo habíamos conseguido para el invierno, y ahora no tenemos nada."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nobody fights them. Go and ask what they want for it!"
msgstr "Nadie lucha contra ellos. ¡Id a preguntar qué quieren a cambio!"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil for oil? No, no. My sail is torn to rags."
msgstr "¿Aceite por aceite? No, no. Mi vela está hecha jirones."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a new sail, and you get your oil back."
msgstr "Traedme una vela nueva y recuperaréis vuestro aceite."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The sailmaker of Durrës makes the best sails."
msgstr "El maestro velero de Durrës hace las mejores velas."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A new sail! Fine work. Here is your oil, captain."
msgstr ""
"¡Una vela nueva! Buen trabajo. Aquí tenéis vuestro aceite, "
"{crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And tell the Aga that Crooked Mast is not his friend."
msgstr "Y decidle al Aga que Mástil Torcido no es su amigo."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sail? Gladly, but my cough is so bad, I can not work."
msgstr "¿Una vela? Con gusto, pero tengo tanta tos que no puedo trabajar."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Only the honey of Vlorë helps."
msgstr "Solo me ayuda la miel de Vlorë."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a jar of honey!"
msgstr "¡Traedme un tarro de miel!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey from Vlorë! My cough is gone already."
msgstr "¡Miel de Vlorë! Ya se me ha pasado la tos."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the sail. The finest in the Adriatic!"
msgstr "Aquí tenéis la vela. ¡La mejor del Adriático!"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey? My bees made plenty."
msgstr "¿Miel? Mis abejas han hecho mucha."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my cheese. Do you have salt on board?"
msgstr "Pero necesito sal para mi queso. ¿Tenéis sal a bordo?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Just what I needed."
msgstr "¡Sal! Justo lo que necesitaba."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is a jar of my best honey."
msgstr "Aquí tenéis un tarro de mi mejor miel."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the olive oil home to {port}."
msgstr "Llevad el aceite de oliva a casa, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our oil! Now we have enough for the winter."
msgstr "¡Nuestro aceite! Ahora tenemos bastante para el invierno."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast sent a message, too:"
msgstr "Mástil Torcido también os manda un mensaje:"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"The Aga's scribe sails south with a heavy book. Watch out for him!\""
msgstr "«El escriba del Aga navega hacia el sur con un libro muy pesado. ¡Cuidado con él!»"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Corsairs of Ulcinj"
msgstr "Los corsarios de Ulcinj"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The corsairs took the villages' olive oil. Find out what they want, and trade it back."
msgstr ""
"Los corsarios se llevaron el aceite de oliva de los pueblos. Descubrid qué quieren y recuperadlo "
"con un intercambio."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The olive trees of the Adriatic grow very old: near Bar in Montenegro stands an olive tree which "
"is said to be more than two thousand years old."
msgstr ""
"Los olivos del Adriático llegan a ser muy viejos: cerca de Bar, en Montenegro, hay un olivo que, "
"según dicen, tiene más de dos mil años."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oil is home!"
msgstr "¡El aceite está en casa!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Not a single shot was fired: a sail, a jar of honey and a sack of salt did it."
msgstr "Sin disparar ni un tiro: lo lograron una vela, un tarro de miel y un saco de sal."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Even the corsair captain is your friend now."
msgstr "Hasta el capitán corsario es ahora vuestro amigo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax!"
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, el Aga quiere las naranjas de Parga como impuesto!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eleni of Parga hid the harvest from his men."
msgstr "Eleni de Parga escondió la cosecha a los hombres del Aga."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Help her get the oranges to the market of Corfu, so that the money stays with the people."
msgstr ""
"Ayudadla a llevar las naranjas al mercado de Corfú, para que el dinero se quede con la gente."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges are ripe, but the Aga's men broke all my baskets."
msgstr "Las naranjas están maduras, pero los hombres del Aga rompieron todas mis cestas."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me baskets! Ilir of Vlorë weaves the best ones."
msgstr "¡Traedme cestas! Ilir de Vlorë teje las mejores."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine baskets! Here are the oranges, captain."
msgstr ""
"¡Qué cestas tan buenas! Aquí tenéis las naranjas, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Smell them: the sun of Parga is inside."
msgstr "Oledlas: dentro está el sol de Parga."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave baskets from the reeds of the lagoon."
msgstr "Tejo cestas con los juncos de la laguna."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But my boat lost its rope. Spiros in Corfu has ropes!"
msgstr "Pero mi barca perdió su cuerda. ¡Spiros, en Corfú, tiene cuerdas!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good rope! Here are my baskets."
msgstr "¡Una buena cuerda! Aquí tenéis mis cestas."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope for Ilir? The harbour of Corfu has ropes for everybody."
msgstr "¿Una cuerda para Ilir? El puerto de Corfú tiene cuerdas para todos."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this one, captain."
msgstr "Tomad esta, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the oranges to the market of {port}."
msgstr "Llevad las naranjas al mercado de {port}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oranges from Parga! The whole market smells of them."
msgstr "¡Naranjas de Parga! Todo el mercado huele a ellas."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The money goes to the people of Parga, not to the Aga."
msgstr "El dinero es para la gente de Parga, no para el Aga."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every orange was sold, and Parga keeps its money."
msgstr "Se vendieron todas las naranjas, y Parga se queda con su dinero."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga gets only the peels!"
msgstr "¡El Aga solo se queda con las cáscaras!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Oranges of Parga"
msgstr "Las naranjas de Parga"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax. Trade your way to baskets and bring the oranges to "
"the market of Corfu."
msgstr ""
"El Aga quiere las naranjas de Parga como impuesto. Haced intercambios hasta conseguir cestas y "
"llevad las naranjas al mercado de Corfú."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Parga was a little Venetian town on the Greek coast for almost 400 years, with Ottoman lands all "
"around it, and it was often raided by its neighbours."
msgstr ""
"Parga fue una pequeña ciudad veneciana en la costa griega durante casi 400 años, rodeada de "
"tierras otomanas, y sus vecinos la asaltaban a menudo."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sweet oranges for Corfu!"
msgstr "¡Naranjas dulces para Corfú!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges reached the market, and the money stayed in Parga."
msgstr "Las naranjas llegaron al mercado, y el dinero se quedó en Parga."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope, a basket and a lot of sailing did it."
msgstr "Lo lograron una cuerda, una cesta y mucho navegar."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the warning of Crooked Mast came true!"
msgstr "¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, el aviso de Mástil Torcido era cierto!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe was here with a heavy book: the ledger of the double taxes."
msgstr ""
"El escriba del Aga estuvo aquí con un libro pesado: el libro de cuentas de los impuestos dobles."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "With it, we can prove everything. But he fled in a hurry. Chase him!"
msgstr "Con él, podemos demostrarlo todo. Pero huyó a toda prisa. ¡Perseguidlo!"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The scribe had {hallmark}."
msgstr "El escriba tenía {hallmark@acc}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Aga's scribe with a heavy book?"
msgstr "¿Habéis visto al escriba del Aga con un libro pesado?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, hiding among the people of the harbour! But which one is he?"
msgstr "¡Está aquí, escondido entre la gente del puerto! Pero ¿cuál es?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the Aga's scribe?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es el escriba del Aga?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the scribe! Remember all four things you learned."
msgstr "¡No, ese no es el escriba! Recordad las cuatro cosas que habéis descubierto."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Alright, alright! Here is the ledger. I only wrote what the Aga told me!\""
msgstr "«¡Vale, vale! Aquí tenéis el libro de cuentas. ¡Yo solo escribía lo que me decía el Aga!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"I will tell the truth before the judge, I promise.\""
msgstr "«Diré la verdad ante el juez, lo prometo.»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger proves it: the Aga took every tax twice!"
msgstr "El libro de cuentas lo demuestra: ¡el Aga cobraba cada impuesto dos veces!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Forged Ledger"
msgstr "El libro de cuentas falso"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe flees with the ledger of the double taxes. Chase him along the coast!"
msgstr ""
"El escriba del Aga huye con el libro de cuentas de los impuestos dobles. ¡Perseguidlo por la "
"costa!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Spectacles were made in Venice from about 1300 on; the glassmakers of Murano were so precious that"
" they were not allowed to leave the republic."
msgstr ""
"En Venecia se hacían gafas desde alrededor de 1300; los vidrieros de Murano eran tan valiosos que "
"no podían salir de la república."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger is yours!"
msgstr "¡El libro de cuentas es vuestro!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You chased the scribe along the whole coast and found him."
msgstr "Perseguisteis al escriba por toda la costa y lo encontrasteis."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the crew holds the proof of the double taxes."
msgstr "Ahora la tripulación tiene la prueba de los impuestos dobles."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, I must confess something."
msgstr "{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, tengo que confesaros algo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I wrote the list of the villages in the old Glagolitic letters, so that the Aga could not read it."
msgstr ""
"Escribí la lista de los pueblos con las antiguas letras glagolíticas, para que el Aga no pudiera "
"leerla."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now I can not read it either! Find a priest who knows the old letters."
msgstr "¡Y ahora yo tampoco puedo leerla! Encontrad a un sacerdote que conozca las letras antiguas."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The priest has {hallmark}."
msgstr "El sacerdote tiene {hallmark@acc}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen a priest who knows the old letters?"
msgstr "¿Habéis visto a un sacerdote que conozca las letras antiguas?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur is here, at the market! But which one is he?"
msgstr "¡Don Grgur está aquí, en el mercado! Pero ¿cuál es?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Don Grgur? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "¿Cuál es Don Grgur? ¡Recordad lo que os dijo la gente!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not him! Think of all three things you learned."
msgstr "¡No, ese no es! Pensad en las tres cosas que habéis descubierto."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Yes, I read the old letters. Let me see... every village, and every ducat!\""
msgstr "«Sí, sé leer las letras antiguas. A ver... ¡cada pueblo y cada ducado!»"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the list back to the scribe in {port}."
msgstr "Llevad la lista de vuelta al escriba {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every village and every ducat, written clearly at last!"
msgstr "¡Cada pueblo y cada ducado, por fin bien claro!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge can give back every coin."
msgstr "Ahora el juez puede devolver cada moneda."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is ready for the judge."
msgstr "La lista ya está preparada para el juez."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will never write in a secret script again!"
msgstr "¡Nunca más escribiré con letras secretas!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Secret Script"
msgstr "La escritura secreta"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The list of the villages is written in old Glagolitic letters. Find a priest who can read it."
msgstr ""
"La lista de los pueblos está escrita con antiguas letras glagolíticas. Encontrad a un sacerdote "
"que sepa leerla."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Glagolitic is the oldest known Slavic alphabet. On the islands of Kvarner, like Krk, and on the "
"islands near Zadar, Croatian priests and scribes kept writing in it for centuries."
msgstr ""
"El glagolítico es el alfabeto eslavo más antiguo que se conoce. En las islas del Kvarner, como "
"Krk, y en las islas cerca de Zadar, los sacerdotes y escribas croatas siguieron escribiendo con él"
" durante siglos."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is read!"
msgstr "¡La lista está leída!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur read the old letters for you."
msgstr "Don Grgur os leyó las letras antiguas."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge will know every village and every ducat."
msgstr "Ahora el juez conocerá cada pueblo y cada ducado."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the judge wants to hear witnesses, not only the ledger."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, el juez quiere oír a testigos, no solo ver el libro "
"de cuentas."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast in Ulcinj, Mustafa in Castelnuovo and Jele in Kotor saw what the Aga's men did."
msgstr ""
"Mástil Torcido en Ulcinj, Mustafa en Castelnuovo y Jele en Kotor vieron lo que hicieron los "
"hombres del Aga."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring all three to Corfu, where the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "¡Llevad a los tres a Corfú, donde empieza el viaje hacia el juez!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Me, a witness? Ha! Fine."
msgstr "¿Yo, testigo? ¡Ja! Vale."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I saw the Aga's men take a tax twice, right at sea."
msgstr "Vi a los hombres del Aga cobrar un impuesto dos veces, en pleno mar."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I keep the gate of Castelnuovo."
msgstr "Yo guardo la puerta de Castelnuovo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every cart of the Aga's men went through it, twice."
msgstr "Todos los carros de los hombres del Aga pasaron por ella, dos veces."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They took my olives as a tax, and came back a week later for more."
msgstr "Se llevaron mis aceitunas como impuesto y una semana después volvieron a por más."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judge everything."
msgstr "Se lo contaré todo al juez."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#: data/missions/34_through_the_bura/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pick up {count} more {count|witness|witnesses}."
msgstr "Recoged {count} testigos más."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "Llevad a los testigos {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast? A corsair as a witness... the judge will be surprised!"
msgstr "¿Mástil Torcido? Un corsario como testigo... ¡el juez se va a sorprender!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Mustafa, the gatekeeper. Welcome to Corfu!"
msgstr "Mustafa, el guardián de la puerta. ¡Bienvenido a Corfú!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Jele of Kotor. Rest a little, the voyage is long."
msgstr "Jele de Kotor. Descansa un poco, el viaje es largo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The witnesses are ready, and so is the ledger."
msgstr "Los testigos están listos, y el libro de cuentas también."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Soon, the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "¡Pronto empieza el viaje hacia el juez!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Witnesses"
msgstr "Los testigos"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The judge wants to hear witnesses. Bring them from Ulcinj, Castelnuovo and Kotor to Corfu."
msgstr "El juez quiere oír a testigos. Traedlos de Ulcinj, Castelnuovo y Kotor a Corfú."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Republic of Ragusa banned the slave trade in 1416. It valued freedom very highly: the word "
"Libertas stands on its flag."
msgstr ""
"La República de Ragusa prohibió el comercio de esclavos en 1416. Valoraba mucho la libertad: en su"
" bandera pone «Libertas»."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The witnesses are ready!"
msgstr "¡Los testigos están listos!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A corsair, a gatekeeper and an olive grower will speak before the judge."
msgstr "Un corsario, un guardián y una cultivadora de olivos hablarán ante el juez."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's days as a tax collector are numbered."
msgstr "Los días del Aga como recaudador de impuestos están contados."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the day has come!"
msgstr "¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, ha llegado el día!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to the kadı of Preveza: he judges by the law."
msgstr "Llevad el libro de cuentas y a los testigos al cadí de Preveza: él juzga según la ley."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Master Ivan waits in Parga, and Doctor Marin is here in Corfu."
msgstr "El maestro Ivan espera en Parga, y el doctor Marin está aquí, en Corfú."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I am ready, captain. I will tell the judge about the fever."
msgstr "Estoy listo, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}. Le hablaré al juez de la fiebre."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! I came all the way from Pula."
msgstr "¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}! He venido desde Pula."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judge about the Aga's recruiter."
msgstr "Le hablaré al juez del reclutador del Aga."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "Llevad el libro de cuentas y a los testigos {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Peace be with you. Show me the ledger, and let the witnesses speak."
msgstr "La paz sea con vosotros. Enseñadme el libro de cuentas y que hablen los testigos."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
