#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#: data/missions/35_peace_of_rijeka/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hmm, no. Think about your voyage, captain."
msgstr "Mmm, no. Pensad en vuestro viaje, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The law is clear. The Aga must give back every double tax, and he loses his post."
msgstr "La ley está clara. El Aga debe devolver cada impuesto doble, y pierde su puesto."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He may go home and look after his goats."
msgstr "Puede irse a casa a cuidar de sus cabras."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres data/missions/35_peace_of_rijeka/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sail home to {port}!"
msgstr "¡Navegad a casa, {port@to}!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You are home, captain! The whole Adriatic heard the news."
msgstr ""
"¡Estáis en casa, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}! Todo el Adriático se ha enterado."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody came to the Arena: the children of Grebaštica, Master Ivan and Katarina,"
msgstr "Todos vinieron a la Arena: los niños de Grebaštica, el maestro Ivan y Katarina,"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Juraj, Doctor Marin, and even Crooked Mast!"
msgstr "Juraj, el doctor Marin, ¡y hasta Mástil Torcido!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres data/missions/35_peace_of_rijeka/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, for your courage you get the medal of the Bird Dog!"
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, por vuestro valor recibís la medalla del Bird Dog!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Kadı of Preveza"
msgstr "El cadí de Preveza"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to the judge in Preveza, then sail home to Pula."
msgstr ""
"Llevad el libro de cuentas y a los testigos ante el juez de Preveza, y luego volved a casa, a "
"Pula."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In the Ottoman Empire, a kadı judged by the law, and the people could bring a complaint even "
"against a powerful aga."
msgstr ""
"En el Imperio otomano, un cadí juzgaba según la ley, y la gente podía presentar una queja incluso "
"contra un aga poderoso."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The voyage is complete!"
msgstr "¡El viaje ha terminado!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga gave back the double taxes, and the villages are free."
msgstr "El Aga devolvió los impuestos dobles, y los pueblos son libres."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The bell of Grebaštica rings, and the whole Arena of Pula cheers!"
msgstr "¡La campana de Grebaštica suena y toda la Arena de Pula aplaude!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, a pigeon came from Bari, with a letter from Luka, the ship's boy!"
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, ha llegado una paloma de Bari con una carta de Luka,"
" el grumete!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He writes: \"A Count has come to Italy, Count Malvento. He shows a Golden Charter.\""
msgstr "Escribe: «Ha llegado a Italia un conde, el conde Malvento. Enseña una Carta de Oro.»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"He takes a toll in every harbour, from Comacchio to Otranto!\""
msgstr "«¡Cobra un peaje en cada puerto, de Comacchio a Otranto!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"His men even took the eel nets of Comacchio as a toll. Please help!\""
msgstr ""
"«Sus hombres hasta se llevaron las redes de anguilas de Comacchio como peaje. ¡Ayudad, por favor!»"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Count's men with the eel nets?"
msgstr "¿Habéis visto a los hombres del conde con las redes de anguilas?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which boat is the Count's? Remember its sail and its hull!"
msgstr "¿Cuál es el barco del conde? ¡Recordad su vela y su casco!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres data/missions/26_caps_too_new/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, not this one! Think of the sail and the hull."
msgstr "¡No, ese no! Pensad en la vela y en el casco."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"That's the one! The Count's men shrug: \"The Count says nets are a toll.\" But they give them "
"back."
msgstr ""
"¡Ese es! Los hombres del conde se encogen de hombros: «El conde dice que las redes son un peaje.» "
"Pero las devuelven."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the eel nets home to {port}."
msgstr "Llevad las redes de anguilas a casa, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our nets! Now we can catch the eels again."
msgstr "¡Nuestras redes! Ya podemos volver a pescar anguilas."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tonight, the whole lagoon eats eels!"
msgstr "¡Esta noche toda la laguna come anguilas!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But this Count... Nobody here ever heard of him before."
msgstr "Pero ese conde... Aquí nadie había oído hablar de él."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Who is he really, captain?"
msgstr "¿Quién es en realidad, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}?"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nets of Comacchio"
msgstr "Las redes de Comacchio"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first crossing to Italy. The Count's men took the eel nets of Comacchio \"as a toll\". Follow "
"their boat and give the nets back."
msgstr ""
"La primera travesía a Italia. Los hombres del conde se llevaron las redes de anguilas de Comacchio"
" «como peaje». Seguid su barco y devolved las redes."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The eels of Comacchio are born far away, in the Sargasso Sea across the ocean, and swim all the "
"way to the lagoon. Nobody knew it in 1600: it was found out only around 1920."
msgstr ""
"Las anguilas de Comacchio nacen muy lejos, en el mar de los Sargazos, al otro lado del océano, y "
"nadan hasta la laguna. En 1600 nadie lo sabía: se descubrió hacia 1920."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The nets are home!"
msgstr "¡Las redes están en casa!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You crossed the sea and found the Count's boat."
msgstr "Cruzasteis el mar y encontrasteis el barco del conde."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The eel fishers of Comacchio can fish again."
msgstr "Los pescadores de anguilas de Comacchio pueden volver a pescar."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count sells \"wind charms\" to the fishermen of this coast."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}, el conde vende «amuletos del viento» a los pescadores"
" de esta costa."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He says that without his charm, no boat gets a good wind!"
msgstr "¡Dice que sin su amuleto ningún barco tiene buen viento!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me three charms, from Rimini, Fano and Ancona. Let us see what is inside."
msgstr "Traedme tres amuletos, de Rímini, Fano y Ancona. Veamos qué hay dentro."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here, take my charm. Three ducats, and still no wind!"
msgstr "Tomad mi amuleto. ¡Tres ducados, y ni un soplo de viento!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "It is only a little bottle with a cork."
msgstr "Solo es una botellita con un corcho."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My husband paid two ducats for this charm."
msgstr "Mi marido pagó dos ducados por este amuleto."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Shake it: nothing inside! Take it."
msgstr "Agitadlo: ¡no hay nada dentro! Lleváoslo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's men sold it to me on the pier."
msgstr "Los hombres del conde me lo vendieron en el muelle."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take it, captain. It never helped me."
msgstr "Lleváoslo, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}. Nunca me sirvió de nada."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Collect {count} more wind {count|charm|charms}."
msgstr "Reunid {count} {count|amuleto|amuletos} del viento más."

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! So you collected my wind charms?"
msgstr "¡Ja! ¿Así que habéis reunido mis amuletos del viento?"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My yellow boat has the best charm of all. Nobody beats it!"
msgstr "Mi barco amarillo tiene el mejor amuleto de todos. ¡Nadie lo vence!"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Race me around the three buoys, in front of the fishermen of Fano!"
msgstr "¡Corred contra mí alrededor de las tres boyas, ante los pescadores de Fano!"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Back for more? The wind still loves me!"
msgstr "¿Volvéis a por más? ¡El viento todavía me quiere!"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Again, around the three buoys!"
msgstr "¡Otra vez, alrededor de las tres boyas!"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "What? You beat my charm boat?"
msgstr "¿Qué? ¿Habéis vencido a mi barco del amuleto?"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bah! The wind was... wrong today."
msgstr "¡Bah! Hoy el viento estaba... raro."

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The fishermen of Fano cheer: skill wins, not charms!"
msgstr "Los pescadores de Fano aplauden: ¡gana la destreza, no los amuletos!"

#. what the crew hears when a rival won the race, one short sentence
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! The wind loves me! The fishermen ask for a rematch tomorrow."
msgstr "¡Ja! ¡El viento me quiere! Los pescadores piden la revancha mañana."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Skill wins, not charms! Nobody in Fano buys a wind charm any more."
msgstr "¡Gana la destreza, no los amuletos! En Fano ya nadie compra amuletos del viento."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "We opened them all: empty bottles, every one!"
msgstr "Los abrimos todos: ¡todos eran botellas vacías!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wind Seller"
msgstr "El vendedor de viento"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
