#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Count dares the crew to a regatta of thirteen boats, as the thirteen knights of 1503. He "
"cheats through the shallows; the crew wins fairly."
msgstr ""
"El conde reta a la tripulación a una regata de trece barcos, como los trece caballeros de 1503. Él"
" hace trampa por los bajíos; la tripulación gana limpiamente."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Challenge of Barletta in 1503 began with an insult at a dinner: a French knight said that the "
"Italians were poor knights. Thirteen knights of each side met in a tournament, and the Italians "
"won."
msgstr ""
"El Desafío de Barletta de 1503 empezó con un insulto en una cena: un caballero francés dijo que "
"los italianos eran malos caballeros. Trece caballeros de cada bando se enfrentaron en un torneo, y"
" ganaron los italianos."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A fair win!"
msgstr "¡Una victoria limpia!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count cut through the shallows, and still you won."
msgstr "El conde atajó por los bajíos, y aun así ganasteis."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "All of Barletta saw who sails fairly."
msgstr "Toda Barletta vio quién navega limpio."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! It's me, Luka, the ship's boy. Remember?"
msgstr "¡{crew|Capitán|Capitana|Capitanes|Capitanas}! Soy yo, Luka, el grumete. ¿Os acordáis?"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count bought up all the olive oil, and he sells it at three times the price."
msgstr "El conde compró todo el aceite de oliva y lo vende tres veces más caro."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But Vito of Monopoli hid some olives. Help him press them!"
msgstr "Pero Vito de Monopoli escondió unas aceitunas. ¡Ayudadle a prensarlas!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this salt along: on this coast, salt buys almost anything."
msgstr "Llevaos esta sal: en esta costa, con sal se compra casi de todo."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My olives are picked, but the Count's men took my pressing mats."
msgstr ""
"Mis aceitunas están recogidas, pero los hombres del conde se llevaron mis capachos de prensar."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Without mats, the press gives no oil. Donata of Brindisi weaves them!"
msgstr "Sin capachos, la prensa no da aceite. ¡Donata de Brindisi los teje!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine mats! The press is turning..."
msgstr "¡Buenos capachos! La prensa ya gira..."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the oil, captain. Take it to the market of Bari."
msgstr ""
"Aquí está el aceite, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}. Llevadlo al mercado de Bari."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave pressing mats from rushes."
msgstr "Tejo capachos de prensar con juncos."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my fish. Do you have salt?"
msgstr "Pero necesito sal para mi pescado. ¿Tenéis sal?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Now my fish keeps all winter."
msgstr "¡Sal! Ahora mi pescado aguanta todo el invierno."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here are my best pressing mats."
msgstr "Aquí tenéis mis mejores capachos de prensar."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the oil to the market of {port}."
msgstr "Llevad el aceite al mercado de {port}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil from Monopoli, at a fair price!"
msgstr "¡Aceite de Monopoli, a un precio justo!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now everybody in Bari can cook again."
msgstr "Ahora todo el mundo en Bari puede volver a cocinar."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's oil sits in his cellar, and nobody buys it!"
msgstr "El aceite del conde se queda en su bodega, ¡y nadie lo compra!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, I will keep my eyes open for him."
