msgid "The court has heard enough. \"Count Malvento\" is Bepi Sgorbio, a copyist."
msgstr "El tribunal ya ha oído bastante. El «conde Malvento» es Bepi Sgorbio, un copista."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He forged his title and his charter. He pays back every toll, and he is a count no more."
msgstr "Falsificó su título y su carta. Devolverá cada peaje, y ya no es conde."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And for one year, he will copy the papers of this court. Honestly!"
msgstr "Y durante un año copiará los papeles de este tribunal. ¡Honradamente!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The fishermen land their catch for free again, from Comacchio to Otranto!"
msgstr "¡Los pescadores vuelven a descargar su pesca gratis, de Comacchio a Otranto!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Baba Stana sent a pigeon: \"Well done, captain!\""
msgstr "Baba Stana mandó una paloma: «¡Bien hecho, {crew|capitán|capitana|capitanes|capitanas}!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "For your courage, you get the medal of the Bird Dog!"
msgstr "¡Por vuestro valor, recibís la medalla del Bird Dog!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
